# T-1890: [get "name" person] with type annotations verifies runtime evaluation succeeds.
# The @String and @Integer annotations are checked at runtime by TypeAssert;
# the runtime values String("Alice") and Int(30) satisfy these annotations.
# T-1917 is now implemented: [get k c] carries constraint: [$Indexable c k v] with
# resolver: FieldType, so static type precision is wired. See
# tests/corpus/eval/typecheck/warnings/get_call_field_type_mismatch.llt-eval for
# a test that proves FieldType fires statically and produces Type::Str (not Any).
[
  person: [name: "Alice"  age: 30]
  n@String: [get "name" person]
  a@Integer: [get "age" person]
]
=== out
Dict({"person": Dict({"name": String("Alice"), "age": Int(30)}), "n": String("Alice"), "a": Int(30)})
